-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/55-plus-communities/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cheapest 55+ community in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For houses, Lakeside Crossing in Conway starts near $190,000, but it is a land-lease community: you own the home and pay lot rent from about $650 a month. For fee-simple ownership, Woodlake Village in Murrells Inlet runs $260,000 to $379,000 with an HOA around $43 a month, and Myrtle Trace in Conway averages about $305,000 at roughly $90 a month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a Del Webb community in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two. Del Webb at Grande Dunes in Myrtle Beach is sold out and resale-only, with listings from about $440,000 to $659,000, and every owner gets the oceanfront Grande Dunes Ocean Club. Del Webb North Myrtle Beach is the only large 55+ community still building new homes, from about $475,000, with 535 homes planned and a $315 monthly HOA."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does land-lease mean at Lakeside Crossing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You buy and own the house, but you rent the ground under it from Sun Communities, starting near $650 a month. The rent covers the amenity campus, lawn care, and trash, there is no HOA, and buyers must be approved for the lease before closing. The homes cost far less than fee-simple 55+ houses, and the trade is that lot rent continues forever and can rise."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Myrtle Beach 55+ communities are gated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Verified gated: Seasons at Prince Creek West in Murrells Inlet, with controlled access, and Del Webb at Grande Dunes. Most of the area's 55+ communities, including Myrtle Trace and Woodlake Village, are not gated."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does South Carolina tax retirement income?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Lightly. Social Security is not taxed at all, and military retirement pay is 100 percent exempt. Other retirement income gets a deduction of up to $3,000 before 65 and up to $10,000 at 65 and older. A separate age-65 deduction of up to $15,000 per person overlaps with the retirement deduction rather than fully stacking."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens to property taxes at 65 in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"After one full calendar year as a South Carolina resident, the Homestead Exemption removes the first $50,000 of your primary home's market value from property tax at age 65, on top of the owner-occupied 4 percent assessment rate. On a typical Grand Strand home that combination produces some of the lowest tax bills on the East Coast."}}]}</script>
+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/55-plus-communities/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cheapest 55+ community in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For houses, Lakeside Crossing in Conway starts near $190,000, but it is a land-lease community: you own the home and pay lot rent from about $650 a month. For fee-simple ownership, Woodlake Village in Murrells Inlet runs $260,000 to $379,000 with an HOA around $43 a month, and in Myrtle Trace in Conway, homes usually sell for about $300,000, with an HOA fee of $95 a month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a Del Webb community in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two. In Del Webb at Grande Dunes in Myrtle Beach, a house usually sells for about $665,000 and a villa for about $430,000, and the HOA dues include the oceanfront Grande Dunes Ocean Club. Del Webb North Myrtle Beach is the only large 55+ community still building new homes. From October 2025 to September 2026, its new homes from the builder usually sold for about $635,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does land-lease mean at Lakeside Crossing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You buy and own the house, but you rent the ground under it from Sun Communities, starting near $650 a month. The rent covers the amenity campus, lawn care, and trash, there is no HOA, and buyers must be approved for the lease before closing. The homes cost far less than fee-simple 55+ houses, and the trade is that lot rent continues forever and can rise."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Myrtle Beach 55+ communities are gated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In Myrtle Trace, the front entrance on Burning Ridge Road has no gate, and the back entrance on Myrtle Ridge Road has gates. Most of the area's 55+ communities, including Woodlake Village, are not gated. For any other community, ask the HOA how its entrance works today."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does South Carolina tax retirement income?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Lightly. Social Security is not taxed at all, and military retirement pay is 100 percent exempt. Other retirement income gets a deduction of up to $3,000 before 65 and up to $10,000 at 65 and older. A separate age-65 deduction of up to $15,000 per person overlaps with the retirement deduction rather than fully stacking."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens to property taxes at 65 in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"After one full calendar year as a South Carolina resident, the Homestead Exemption removes the first $50,000 of your primary home's market value from property tax at age 65, on top of the owner-occupied 4 percent assessment rate. On a typical Grand Strand home that combination produces some of the lowest tax bills on the East Coast."}}]}</script>
