+<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">Combining VA loan with a DPA program without understanding the rate impact</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>Down payment help can change the rate on the first mortgage. SC Housing offers a lower rate on some of its loans taken without its down payment help. Before you add down payment help to a VA loan, ask your lender to quote the loan both ways. Compare the total cost over the years you expect to keep the home.</p></div></div>
+<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">Underestimating the VA funding fee</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>Most VA borrowers pay a one-time VA funding fee at closing, a percentage of the loan that varies with first or subsequent use and with any down payment you choose to make; putting more down shrinks it. Disabled veterans with a service-connected disability rating are exempt. This fee can be rolled into the loan but adds to your total loan balance. Factor it into your total cost of purchase.</p></div></div>
